DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council New York Fellowship 2027 (USD 38\,
 000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's New York Fellowship brings artists
 \, scholars and arts professionals from Asia to New York City for a six-mo
 nth immersive cultural exchange. SUPPORT: USD 38\,000 for the six-month fe
 llowship. ELIGIBILITY: non-US citizens/residents from ACC-eligible Asian c
 ountries (including Bangladesh\, Cambodia\, China\, Hong Kong\, India\, In
 donesia\, Japan\, Korea\, Malaysia\, Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakistan
 \, Philippines\, Singapore\, Sri Lanka\, Taiwan\, Thailand and Vietnam\, a
 mong others)\; age 21+\; at least five years of professional experience in
  an eligible discipline (architecture\, archaeology\, art history\, arts a
 dministration\, arts criticism\, conservation\, crafts\, curation\, dance\
 , ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum studies\, music\, theater\,
  visual art)\; English proficiency (J-1 visa requirement)\; fellows cannot
  work or pursue coursework during the fellowship. COHORTS: January-June 20
 28 or July-December 2028. HOW TO APPLY: via the GoApply platform\; applica
 tions open 1 October 2026. Recommendation letters due 16 November 2026. No
  application fee. DEADLINE: 10 November 2026 at 9:59 AM ET.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Asian Cultural Council\nLocation: Six-month fellowship in New York City
 . For artists\, scholars and arts professionals from ACC-eligible Asian co
 untries (non-US citizens/residents).\nAward: USD 38\,000 for the six-month
  fellowship\, covering the immersive cultural exchange in New York City. N
 o application fee.\nDuration: Six months\, in one of two cohorts: January-
 June 2028 or July-December 2028\n\nMore: https://www.asianculturalcouncil.
 org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Six-month fellowship in New York City. For artists\, scholars and 
 arts professionals from ACC-eligible Asian countries (non-US citizens/resi
 dents).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acc-individual-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council Individual Fellowship 2027 (up to 
 USD 35\,000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's Individual Fellowship supports sel
 f-directed exploration and cultural exchange experiences in a new or less 
 familiar environment\, fostering exchange between the United States and As
 ia and within Asia. SUPPORT: up to USD 35\,000 for a 1-to-6-month program 
 (minimum 30 days\; two or more months preferred)\; single or joint applica
 tions with up to 3 participants. ELIGIBILITY: citizens or permanent reside
 nts of ACC-eligible countries (the US and countries across Asia\, from Afg
 hanistan to Vietnam)\; age 21+\; at least five years of professional exper
 ience in an eligible discipline (architecture\, archaeology\, art history\
 , arts administration\, arts criticism\, conservation\, crafts\, curation\
 , dance\, ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum studies\, music\, t
 heater\, visual art)\; English proficiency if traveling to the US\; no cou
 rsework or teaching during the fellowship. Grant activities must take plac
 e between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2028. HOW TO APPLY: via the GoAppl
 y platform\; applications open 1 October 2026. Recommendation letters due 
 16 November 2026. No application fee. DEADLINE: 10 November 2026 at 9:59 A
 M ET.\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council\nLocation: Self-directed cul
 tural exchange between the US and Asia\, or within Asia. For citizens and 
 permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries (including the US).\nAward: 
 Up to USD 35\,000 for self-directed exploration and cultural exchange of 1
  to 6 months. Single or joint applications (up to 3 participants). No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: 1 to 6 months (minimum 30 days\; 2 or more months 
 preferred)\, with grant activities between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2
 028\n\nMore: https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Self-directed cultural exchange between the US and Asia\, or withi
 n Asia. For citizens and permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries (in
 cluding the US).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mplus-sigg-fellowship-chinese-art-research-2026-27@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Deadline: M+ Sigg Fellowship for Chinese Art Research 2026/27 (HKD 
 200\,000\, Hong Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Sigg Fellowship for Chinese Art Research supports new resea
 rch on Chinese art in dialogue with the M+ Collections\; the 2026/27 editi
 on focuses on tradition and contemporary Chinese art. WHO: individuals or 
 research groups of any nationality and any age\, with a postgraduate degre
 e in a relevant discipline\, or an undergraduate degree plus at least thre
 e years of relevant professional or academic research experience\; profici
 ency in spoken and written Chinese or English is required\, and the fellow
 ship is subject to obtaining a Hong Kong visa. WHAT YOU GET: HKD 200\,000 
 to cover all expenses\, including travel\, living\, insurance and research
  costs\, for a three-to-six-month attachment to M+. Fellows give a public 
 lecture in Hong Kong and write an essay of at least 5\,000 English words o
 r 7\,500 Chinese characters for M+ Magazine. APPLICATION: submit a researc
 h proposal (max 1\,000 words) and full CV via the Google form on the call 
 page\, in English or Chinese\, and have two academic or professional refer
 ees email recommendation letters directly. Results are announced in early 
 2027. DEADLINE: 30 November 2026\, 23:59 (UTC+8).\n\nOrganisation: M+\, We
 st Kowloon Cultural District\nLocation: Hong Kong. Open to individuals or 
 research groups of any nationality\; the fellowship depends on obtaining a
  Hong Kong visa.\nAward: HKD 200\,000 covering all expenses (travel\, livi
 ng\, insurance and research costs). No application fee mentioned.\nDuratio
 n: 3 to 6 months attached to M+ in Hong Kong.\n\nMore: https://www.mplus.o
 rg.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/sigg-fellowship-for-chinese-art-research/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mplus.org.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/sigg-fellowship-for-
 chinese-art-research/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
LOCATION:Hong Kong. Open to individuals or research groups of any nationali
 ty\; the fellowship depends on obtaining a Hong Kong visa.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:parc-palestinian-research-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261206
SUMMARY:Deadline: PARC Palestinian Research Fellowship 2027-2028 (up to USD
  6\,000\, arts\, humanities and social sciences)
DESCRIPTION:PARC's 28th annual fellowship competition for Palestinian schol
 ars funds field-based research in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\
 , public health and environmental studies\; purely scientific research is 
 not eligible. WHO: Palestinian PhD students who have defended their disser
 tation proposal\, or Palestinian PhD holders\, regardless of residence or 
 ID\; researchers without a doctorate qualify with at least 10 refereed art
 icles\, and MA holders only as part of a team led by a PhD holder. Recent 
 PARC fellows (last three years) are ineligible. FIELDWORK: in Palestine\, 
 Jordan\, Egypt or Lebanon\, lasting two months to one year (Golan Heights 
 proposals accepted with a comparative Palestine framework). WHAT YOU GET: 
 up to USD 6\,000\, with research to be completed by 31 December 2028. APPL
 ICATION: in English via the Apply Now link (application form\, 350-word ab
 stract\, 2\,000-word proposal\, service component\, budget\, CV up to 10 p
 ages\, ID and passport details\; PhD students also transcripts and two rec
 ommendation letters). Information webinar 27 October 2026\; awards announc
 ed 15 April 2027. DEADLINE: 5 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Palestinian 
 American Research Center (PARC)\nLocation: For Palestinian researchers reg
 ardless of residence or ID\; fieldwork in Palestine\, Jordan\, Egypt or Le
 banon.\nAward: Up to USD 6\,000 per fellowship (tuition not covered). No a
 pplication fee mentioned.\nDuration: 2 to 12 months of fieldwork\; researc
 h to be completed by 31 December 2028.\n\nMore: https://www.parc-us-pal.or
 g/fellowships-for-palestinians/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://www.parc-us-pal.org/fellowships-for-palestinians/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For Palestinian researchers regardless of residence or ID\; fieldw
 ork in Palestine\, Jordan\, Egypt or Lebanon.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:doma-british-council-venice-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Deadline: DOMA Initiatives x British Council: Venice Biennale Fello
 wship 2027 (Malaysia\, GBP 5\,050)
DESCRIPTION:DOMA Initiatives\, in partnership with the British Council\, no
 minates one Malaysia-based fellow for the British Council Venice Fellowshi
 p Programme at the 2027 Venice Biennale (62nd International Art Exhibition
 ). The fellow spends one month in Venice: half the time as an exhibition a
 mbassador at the British Pavilion (stewarding\, engaging visitors\, suppor
 ting daily gallery operations) and half on independent research or a creat
 ive or architectural project inspired by Venice\, the Pavilion and the Bie
 nnale themes. Fellows complete 15 hours of online training in March-April 
 2027 and\, on return\, run a sharing session\, workshop or exhibition for 
 DOMA Initiatives. ELIGIBILITY: active early-career professionals in archit
 ecture or related creative fields\, based in Malaysia\, with a portfolio i
 ntegrating research or creative practice with the themes of La Biennale di
  Venezia\; strong spoken and written English\; must also meet the British 
 Council criteria in the Venice Fellowship Programme Guidance Notes 2027. H
 OW TO APPLY: complete the application form (Google Doc linked from the cal
 l page) and email it with a CV and portfolio/research proposal to the sele
 ction committee. Shortlisting and interviews 30 November to 3 December 202
 6\; nomination to the British Council 4 December 2026\; final selection an
 nounced January 2027. Contact: Veronica Ng\, DOMA Initiatives Coordinator\
 , veronican@sunway.edu.my. DEADLINE: 27 November 2026\, 12:00 noon MYT.\n\
 nOrganisation: DOMA Initiatives\, in partnership with the British Council\
 nLocation: Venice\, Italy (British Pavilion\, 62nd International Art Exhib
 ition). Only for early-career professionals based in Malaysia.\nAward: GBP
  5\,050 fellowship grant covering travel\, accommodation in Venice\, visa 
 processing and daily living expenses. No separate artist fee or honorarium
  beyond this grant. One fellowship place. No application fee mentioned.\nD
 uration: 1 month in Venice between May and November 2027\, plus 15 hours o
 f online pre-fellowship training in March-April 2027\n\nMore: https://www.
 domainitiatives.org/venice2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.domainitiatives.org/venice2027?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Venice\, Italy (British Pavilion\, 62nd International Art Exhibiti
 on). Only for early-career professionals based in Malaysia.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acc-graduate-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council Graduate Fellowship 2027 (USD 15\,
 000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's Graduate Fellowship supports Asian
  graduate students in an eligible arts or culture discipline at a US unive
 rsity. SUPPORT: USD 15\,000 for one academic year of full-time coursework\
 ; a second year may be renewed at ACC's discretion. ELIGIBILITY: citizens 
 or legal permanent residents of an ACC-eligible country\, territory or reg
 ion in Asia (US citizens and permanent residents are not eligible)\; enrol
 led in\, or admitted by 1 April 2027 to\, a full-time in-residence graduat
 e degree in the US in an eligible discipline (architecture\, archaeology\,
  art history\, arts administration\, arts criticism\, conservation\, craft
 s\, curation\, dance\, ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum studie
 s\, music\, theater\, visual art)\; must be in the coursework phase\, not 
 the research or thesis phase. The five-year experience requirement for oth
 er ACC fellowships does not apply. Applicants need a valid US student visa
  (ACC does not sponsor student visas). Applicants may apply to only one AC
 C programme per cycle. HOW TO APPLY: via the GoApply portal with an Indivi
 dual Account (https://goapply2.akoyago.com/acc/application/GRAD2027). Reco
 mmendation letters due 16 November 2026\, 9:59 AM ET. Questions: the ACC o
 ffice matching your citizenship (Hong Kong\, Japan\, Philippines and Taiwa
 n have their own offices\; all others application@accny.org). DEADLINE: 10
  November 2026\, 9:59 AM ET.\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council\nLoca
 tion: Full-time\, in-residence graduate programme in the US. For citizens 
 and permanent residents of ACC-eligible Asian countries (US citizens and p
 ermanent residents not eligible).\nAward: USD 15\,000 for one academic yea
 r\, renewable for a second year at ACC's discretion. No application fee.\n
 Duration: One academic year of full-time coursework (Fall 2027 to Spring 2
 028\, or Spring 2028 to Fall 2028)\n\nMore: https://www.asianculturalcounc
 il.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Full-time\, in-residence graduate programme in the US. For citizen
 s and permanent residents of ACC-eligible Asian countries (US citizens and
  permanent residents not eligible).
END:VEVENT
